{"skill":{"slug":"executing-plans","displayName":"Executing Plans"},"version":{"version":"0.1.0","createdAt":1769580599462,"changelog":"- Initial release of the executing-plans skill.\n- Introduces a structured process: load and review plan, execute tasks in batches, and report progress for feedback.\n- Emphasizes critical review, stopping for clarification on blockers, and not guessing when instructions are unclear.\n- Includes explicit instructions for batch size, checkpoints, and required skill handoff for finishing development.\n- Clearly defines when to pause for help or revisit previous steps based on plan changes or feedback.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2171,"sha256":"582937183ad9bec6fac0ce8c6ad85d2e6404e1e274a4564594577f1965d4d8ae","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1608,"sha256":"a44e69b018f9085ab7acfcbca4664287571076a37874b8fba0e69dfce4f5b307","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789022529478,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"4a3bf7155ee8e9d088d8ece7df28e38c92d04fc0fc1ee2e12cc5174ba87d3aff","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/4a3bf7155ee8e9d088d8ece7df28e38c92d04fc0fc1ee2e12cc5174ba87d3aff","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: executing-plans\nVersion: 0.1.0\n\nThe skill bundle is benign. The `_meta.json` file contains standard metadata. The `SKILL.md` file provides instructions for an AI agent to execute a development plan in batches, emphasizing critical review, verification, reporting, and stopping when blocked. There are no instructions for data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence, or prompt injection aiming for harmful objectives. The use of a sub-skill (`superpowers:finishing-a-development-branch`) is a standard modular approach and not indicative of malicious intent.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160183729},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":17,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"SAFE","issueCount":2,"checkedAt":1789022529478},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a plain workflow guide for executing a written implementation plan in small reviewed batches, with no bundled code, persistence, or hidden data access.","dimensions":[{"detail":"It relies on the agent's existing coding environment and does not request unrelated access to credentials, sessions, private stores, network services, or privileged system areas.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The inspected artifact is a single Markdown skill file with no executable scripts, dependencies, install hooks, or remote payload retrieval.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill is broad because it applies to implementation plans generally, but it includes critical review, blocker stops, verification, and between-batch human checkpoints.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No persistence, background worker, scheduled task, memory-writing behavior, privilege escalation, or tool hijacking is present in the artifact.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The purpose is coherent: it tells an agent to load a plan, review it critically, execute a small batch of tasks, verify work, and report back for review.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you want an agent workflow for executing plans in batches. Review any plan before using it, especially if it includes destructive commands, deployments, secrets, production data, or other high-impact actions.","findings":"[SQP-1] expected: The broad invocation scope is real but aligned with a generic plan-execution skill; artifact instructions require plan review, raising concerns before starting, verification, and stopping on blockers, so it does not create a material Review concern by itself.\n[EA2] unexpected: The cited concern is not supported as stated: the artifact says not to skip verifications and to report between batches and wait for feedback, rather than enabling unchecked autonomous high-impact execution.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789022529478}}}}}